ARCH-05 -- decision_core.py: close the five LATENT cases the adversarial risk battery found.

decision_core.py is money path and is not edited from a research session; this is the patch for
the desktop pass. Apply from the repository root with:

    git apply context/patches/arch05_decision_core_nonfinite.patch

What it changes (each line names the battery case in desks/mt5/research/adversarial_risk.py):
  * implementable_lot: a non-finite target is no target (0.0), and the live handle's
    volume_max bounds the lot                                    -> volume_max_desk_side
  * book_from_allocation: non-finite weights are dropped on both paths -> book_weight_inf
  * cap_by_heat: a non-finite / non-positive allocation is treated as unusable (derived
    budget), and an unreadable venue daily-loss bar admits nothing
                               -> cap_by_heat_direct_nan, cap_by_heat_direct_inf, venue_loss_bar_nan

None of the five is reachable on today's live path (each case names the proof), so none is a
bypass; the patch makes each control's own contract say what the caller already guarantees.
No cap, veto or shrink is added on a finite, well-formed input: every branch fires only on NaN,
infinity, a non-number, or a lot the venue would refuse. Validated 2026-10-07 by running the
battery against a patched copy of mt5desk: PASS, 68 HELD, 0 LATENT.

--- a/desks/mt5/mt5desk/decision_core.py	2026-10-07 06:13:40.674515803 +0000
+++ b/desks/mt5/mt5desk/decision_core.py	2026-10-07 06:14:00.969253895 +0000
@@ -590,9 +590,24 @@
